---
import GuidePage from '../../components/GuidePage.astro';
---

<GuidePage
  title="Use Quilt Fabric Remnants Before Buying More"
  description="Allocate exact project-local remnants first, preserve useful leftovers, and plan only the bolt shortfall."
  eyebrow="Common Workflow"
  guideSlug="use-remnants-before-buying"
  guideCategory="workflow"
>
  <section>
    <h2>Choose remnants for this project</h2><p>
      QuiltClarity is not a stash database. Add only the pieces available for
      this plan, name them clearly, and measure the rectangle you can actually
      cut.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Let assignment affect the purchase</h2><p>
      The stock-aware planner evaluates alternative assignments because using a
      flexible remnant for the wrong piece can increase the bolt length later.
      Lower raw additional purchase is considered before prettier waste.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Keep each execution step identifiable</h2><p>
      Results name each stock bin, show its placed cuts and practical leftover
      rectangles, then show any purchased-fabric layout. Safety is applied only
      to that new purchase.
    </p>
  </section>
  <p>
    <a href="/guides/add-fabric-you-have/">Learn how to enter stock pieces</a>.
  </p>
</GuidePage>
